WEBVTT

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:08.211
Hey, it's morning.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.463
Wake up, boys.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.925
Praetorian…

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.690
<i>Hold on, folks!
Can we zoom in with that shot?</i>

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.318
<i>I knew it! It's him!</i>

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:36.906
<i>Who is the superhero who's come to
San Francisco where a string of assaults</i>

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.324
<i>on jewelry stores has occurred?</i>

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:43.413
<i>It's the enforcer of ancient Rome
revived in the present day, Praetorian!</i>

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:45.874
<i>Of the new generation of superheroes</i>

00:02:45.957 --> 00:02:47.876
<i>of The Union of Justice,</i>

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:50.170
<i>Praetorian's popularity is booming
on the West Coast!</i>

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:54.257
<i>Who'd have thought this popular figure
would show up for this level of robberies?</i>

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.717
<i>What a surprising development!</i>

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.513
<i>The secret of his popularity
is his amazing superpowers!</i>

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.224
<i>While he has 200 different abilities,</i>

00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:06.936
<i>which one he uses each time
is completely random!</i>

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.813
<i>Even Praetorian himself doesn't know!</i>

00:03:09.397 --> 00:03:13.693
<i>He's also a popular subject
among oddsmakers overseas.</i>

00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:16.905
<i>We can hardly wait to see which</i>

00:03:17.488 --> 00:03:19.616
<i>of Praetorian's powers
will manifest today!</i>

00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:27.665
What? Which is it?

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:35.214
This is as far as you go.

00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:39.469
This ain't fair.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.471
We're truly out of luck now.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.097
Yeah.

00:03:43.181 --> 00:03:44.724
Surrender.

00:03:49.771 --> 00:03:50.730
-Scatter!
-Right!

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:58.488
<i>Unbelievable! Right off the bat,
it's the incredible Spark Division!</i>

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.407
<i>Praetorian himself
divides into multiple copies!</i>

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.201
<i>Hold on a second.</i>

00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:08.665
<i>This means that if the four Praetorians
each use their powers at random,</i>

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.459
<i>the possibilities are
200 to the 4th power!</i>

00:04:11.542 --> 00:04:14.087
<i>The possibilities are staggering!</i>

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.922
<i>It's all over for these villains!</i>

00:04:16.005 --> 00:04:19.384
<i>And most of all,
Praetorian is known for having</i>

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.220
<i>absolutely zero mercy on supervillains!</i>

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:44.617
I can take him one-on-one!

00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:44.969
Wait--

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:03.029
Beaten to death.

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:15.917
I've got no choice.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:20.713
May all four of you have bad luck at once!

00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:28.137
He's reflecting it back!

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.443
Fish?

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:45.947
That hurts!

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.323
No way.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:03.881
Crushed to death.

00:07:04.465 --> 00:07:07.927
<i>Incredibly,
he reflected back the bad luck!</i>

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.929
<i>That was his Reflection Wave!</i>

00:07:10.721 --> 00:07:12.056
<i>Poor guy.</i>

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.933
-<i>What's next?</i>
-Yeah!

00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:16.269
Nice, Transmit!

00:07:19.981 --> 00:07:21.357
Okay! Let's go!

00:07:25.194 --> 00:07:27.238
<i>It's Teleport Tension!</i>

00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:29.657
<i>We've got an overlap of powers!</i>

00:07:30.241 --> 00:07:31.534
I did it before, remember?

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:34.412
You're not the only one
who's good at teleporting!

00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:37.039
Yeah.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:55.224
Kicked to death.

00:07:58.769 --> 00:08:00.563
Transmit…

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:19.081
Bring it on!

00:08:20.541 --> 00:08:22.543
The last guy's an electrician, huh?

00:08:22.627 --> 00:08:23.878
Fuck off!

00:08:33.971 --> 00:08:38.851
You ain't taking me
back to prison just yet, bastard!

00:08:40.937 --> 00:08:42.772
Don't underestimate electricity!

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.201
It's time for your punishment.

00:08:55.284 --> 00:08:59.080
Are you kidding me?
Four against one is cowardly!

00:09:04.502 --> 00:09:06.420
It's just the two of us now, punk.

00:09:26.857 --> 00:09:28.693
Hey, you punk villain.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:30.820
What?

00:09:31.821 --> 00:09:33.990
This isn't your first crime, is it?

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:36.367
How long have you
been out of Supermax Prison?

00:09:36.867 --> 00:09:39.203
What do you care?

00:09:40.454 --> 00:09:41.414
How long has it been?

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.458
That's none of your business.

00:09:55.511 --> 00:09:56.679
I got out yesterday.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:59.390
Yesterday? You mean "yesterday" yesterday?

00:09:59.473 --> 00:10:01.475
It's really been less than 24 hours?

00:10:02.393 --> 00:10:03.603
Yeah…

00:10:04.645 --> 00:10:05.980
That's pitiful.

00:10:06.897 --> 00:10:08.316
Yeah, it is pitiful.

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:12.194
That's not fair, is it?

00:10:13.362 --> 00:10:14.363
All right then.

00:10:14.447 --> 00:10:18.326
It's just not fair
to send you back to prison so soon.

00:10:18.409 --> 00:10:20.745
Fair? I don't get it.

00:10:22.038 --> 00:10:24.915
It really isn't fair, is it, punk villain?

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:29.712
I, Praetorian the enforcer,
am a harsh hero.

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:30.671
However,

00:10:31.339 --> 00:10:33.883
I hate the crime, not the criminal.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.428
There's someone in your life
who loves you too, right?

00:10:38.012 --> 00:10:40.181
Well… Yeah, there is.

00:10:44.685 --> 00:10:47.563
You really shouldn't make
that person sad, should you?

00:10:49.732 --> 00:10:51.776
I'll never do anything so stupid again.

00:10:54.111 --> 00:10:55.905
Good. That's a promise, right?

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.198
Huh?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.950
Yeah, I promise.

00:11:01.369 --> 00:11:02.578
You hear that, boys?

00:11:04.664 --> 00:11:06.582
You'll never get this chance again!

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:08.834
Yeah… Of course.

00:11:10.211 --> 00:11:11.295
I swear on my bad luck.

00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:12.296
Yeah.

00:11:12.963 --> 00:11:15.466
Make a fresh start in your lives.

00:11:15.966 --> 00:11:17.426
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

00:11:18.302 --> 00:11:19.720
Farewell, boys!

00:11:28.646 --> 00:11:30.689
So long.

00:11:30.773 --> 00:11:31.732
What was that about?

00:11:31.816 --> 00:11:33.484
-I dunno.
-Yeah.

00:11:38.239 --> 00:11:39.782
You half-wits! Get in!

00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:40.783
Kasey…

00:11:41.909 --> 00:11:42.952
Was that your doing?

00:11:44.078 --> 00:11:45.621
Hurry! The cops will be here soon!

00:12:05.808 --> 00:12:09.270
Ms. Kasey really is amazing,
ain't she, Frost?

00:12:09.353 --> 00:12:13.107
So you can psychically control
anyone you want.

00:12:13.691 --> 00:12:18.571
Controlling even Praetorian without him
knowing it is incredible, ain't it?

00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:20.072
Yeah!

00:12:20.156 --> 00:12:26.245
How come you never told us
Kasey has such an awesome power, Johnny?

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:28.497
Johnny.

00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:31.208
Would you shut up, Frost?

00:12:31.292 --> 00:12:33.377
She saved you,
so keep quiet and be thankful.

00:12:33.461 --> 00:12:35.379
Of course, we are!

00:12:35.463 --> 00:12:39.008
We're totally thankful and impressed
by Kasey honey! Right, Transmit?

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:40.134
Yeah!

00:12:40.718 --> 00:12:42.970
"Kasey honey"? Watch what you say.

00:12:43.554 --> 00:12:46.265
With that kind of power,
we'd be invincible.

00:12:46.348 --> 00:12:47.725
Next time, she's coming with--

00:12:48.309 --> 00:12:49.143
No thanks!

00:12:49.226 --> 00:12:52.688
I was only able to control
that Praetorian out of sheer luck.

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:54.815
That same trick won't work next time.

00:12:54.899 --> 00:12:56.609
That's not true.

00:12:56.692 --> 00:12:58.819
With your superpower, honey, we can do it.

00:13:00.237 --> 00:13:03.741
Every day, he obtains
a different new random power.

00:13:03.824 --> 00:13:08.204
Next time, he might have
the power to defend against my ability.

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:10.206
That's what makes Praetorian dangerous.

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:11.707
Kasey…

00:13:12.583 --> 00:13:14.960
You guys really are total half-wits.

00:13:15.044 --> 00:13:17.588
You're so utterly daft.

00:13:17.671 --> 00:13:18.923
You do zero planning.

00:13:19.006 --> 00:13:21.884
Everything you do is a complete risk.

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:24.303
What's worse,
your haul wasn't even worth it.

00:13:24.887 --> 00:13:27.014
We got 8,000 dollars each!

00:13:27.097 --> 00:13:28.224
Yeah!

00:13:31.227 --> 00:13:35.147
That's not bad for a night's work.
Right, Johnny?

00:13:35.231 --> 00:13:36.065
It sure ain't.

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:41.320
If you guys don't get serious,
you'll end up back in Supermax.

00:13:41.403 --> 00:13:42.905
-You're right, honey!
-Right!

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:12.351
<i>What a surprising development!</i>

00:14:12.434 --> 00:14:14.728
<i>Praetorian's actions were
so full of affection!</i>

00:14:14.812 --> 00:14:16.063
<i>Now that's a real hero!</i>

00:14:16.146 --> 00:14:20.025
<i>Praetorian's popularity has been due
to his harsh punishment…</i>

00:14:20.109 --> 00:14:23.070
Welcome back, Praetorian! Nice work!

00:14:24.947 --> 00:14:28.033
What you did
in San Francisco was so magnificent!

00:14:28.117 --> 00:14:29.994
But why did you let them go?

00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:32.830
I don't know.

00:14:41.505 --> 00:14:43.841
Aw, he's so modest.

00:14:53.934 --> 00:14:55.102
I can't take this.

00:14:55.686 --> 00:14:56.604
Kasey?

00:14:56.687 --> 00:14:59.356
I can't live like this.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.191
I'm sorry.

00:15:01.275 --> 00:15:02.735
But those guys are my--

00:15:02.818 --> 00:15:03.652
Johnny.

00:15:04.778 --> 00:15:05.863
Listen.

00:15:06.572 --> 00:15:11.160
If you keep playing at doing crimes
with those half-wit novice villains,

00:15:11.243 --> 00:15:13.162
I can't deal with it anymore.

00:15:13.245 --> 00:15:16.790
"Playing at doing crimes"?
That's going a little far.

00:15:16.874 --> 00:15:19.335
This means I'm through with you.

00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:21.337
Wait. What do you mean?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:24.506
Exactly like it sounds.
I'm done. We're through.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:28.761
I mean, think about it. You lied to me
and did whatever you pleased.

00:15:29.386 --> 00:15:30.971
You broke your promise too.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:34.183
I'm sorry. But…

00:15:34.266 --> 00:15:37.436
Johnny, you need to use your head more.

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:39.146
What?

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.024
Just look at the supervillain world.

00:15:42.107 --> 00:15:45.069
Don't you see what fate
awaits most of those people?

00:15:46.779 --> 00:15:49.782
The little jobs those half-wits do,

00:15:49.865 --> 00:15:52.117
the majority of guys
who do that kind of stuff

00:15:52.201 --> 00:15:55.704
spend nearly all their lives
inside Supermax. Right?

00:15:56.956 --> 00:15:57.790
Yeah.

00:15:58.374 --> 00:15:59.875
Use your head!

00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:03.963
A real pro supervillain
should pull off a really big job

00:16:04.046 --> 00:16:05.673
and retire as soon as possible.

00:16:06.256 --> 00:16:09.009
Then by efficiently using
the money you make,

00:16:09.093 --> 00:16:12.763
you can live a plain, ordinary,
but extravagant life.

00:16:13.681 --> 00:16:15.099
That's not how a villain lives.

00:16:15.182 --> 00:16:17.810
It's the same as NBA athletes, right?

00:16:18.435 --> 00:16:22.398
After making all they can
during their active career,

00:16:22.481 --> 00:16:24.108
they can live an easy life.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.568
Think about it that way.

00:16:27.695 --> 00:16:29.113
The NBA?

00:16:29.947 --> 00:16:31.198
That's right.

00:16:31.281 --> 00:16:35.536
I work as a socially aware server
with those snobbish dilettantes

00:16:36.036 --> 00:16:40.582
and study to get my MBA
at night school after work

00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:42.876
all just for that moment.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.045
MBA?

00:16:45.129 --> 00:16:46.797
Just once is enough.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.049
If we can succeed at one huge haul,

00:16:49.633 --> 00:16:51.218
then with my preparation,

00:16:51.301 --> 00:16:54.346
I'll manage the investment portfolio
we build with that capital.

00:16:55.431 --> 00:16:58.851
All that stuff about
NBA and MBA means nothing to me.

00:16:59.768 --> 00:17:00.644
But…

00:17:00.728 --> 00:17:02.271
But what?

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:06.525
When is that huge job going to be?
And how will we get it?

00:17:07.776 --> 00:17:08.819
Good question.

00:17:09.611 --> 00:17:11.530
How long will we have to wait?

00:17:12.114 --> 00:17:16.660
And what if our active careers
as villains end before it arrives?

00:17:16.744 --> 00:17:18.495
Fine, Johnny.

00:17:18.579 --> 00:17:20.914
What? Kasey?

00:17:22.583 --> 00:17:23.959
Are you prepared?

00:17:25.919 --> 00:17:29.214
You better believe it.
I'm always prepared.

00:17:29.923 --> 00:17:31.592
All right then, Johnny.

00:17:32.384 --> 00:17:35.596
Do you know who The Heat is?

00:17:36.305 --> 00:17:37.431
The Heat?

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.438
<i>His name is "The Heat."</i>

00:17:44.938 --> 00:17:46.899
<i>In 1970s,</i>

00:17:46.982 --> 00:17:50.360
<i>he was a notorious man
who set numerous criminal records.</i>

00:17:52.821 --> 00:17:55.741
<i>He would hit jewelry stores
and banks one after another,</i>

00:17:57.076 --> 00:17:59.995
<i>steal a car, then make his getaway
over and over again.</i>

00:18:02.289 --> 00:18:04.708
<i>A dangerous criminal
who appeared when least expected,</i>

00:18:05.375 --> 00:18:08.212
<i>he never once killed anyone
in his 45 years as a villain.</i>

00:18:08.796 --> 00:18:11.965
<i>He was considered a hero
by the poor who were under the thumb</i>

00:18:12.049 --> 00:18:13.592
<i>of the powerful at that time.</i>

00:18:14.176 --> 00:18:18.972
<i>He was a fleeting legend
who swept the land during his prime.</i>

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.517
<i>Those who know the true identity</i>

00:18:22.267 --> 00:18:25.395
<i>of this legendary supervillain
are already all in the grave.</i>

00:18:27.314 --> 00:18:28.774
<i>While tricking the superheroes,</i>

00:18:28.857 --> 00:18:33.320
<i>he abruptly disappeared
before anyone could expose him.</i>

00:18:35.364 --> 00:18:37.157
<i>But even now,</i>

00:18:37.241 --> 00:18:39.743
<i>every time rumors of his death spread,</i>

00:18:39.827 --> 00:18:44.456
<i>he has returned again and again
as if to add a new page to his legends.</i>

00:18:45.165 --> 00:18:50.295
<i>This living legend is still talked about
throughout the decades.</i>

00:18:51.004 --> 00:18:53.799
<i>Just when will he make
his next appearance?</i>

00:18:55.592 --> 00:18:57.719
A legendary supervillain, huh?

00:18:57.803 --> 00:18:58.637
Yes.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:01.181
He's my beloved former teacher.

00:19:01.682 --> 00:19:04.351
He taught me all I needed
to survive in this industry.

00:19:05.227 --> 00:19:07.896
So what happened to The Heat?

00:19:09.273 --> 00:19:11.900
What's he got to do with our future?

00:19:11.984 --> 00:19:12.901
Everything.

00:19:13.443 --> 00:19:14.820
Now for the main event.

00:19:15.612 --> 00:19:20.576
<i>The Heat is putting together
a team for a big job</i>

00:19:20.659 --> 00:19:22.578
<i>for an overseas client.</i>

00:19:23.162 --> 00:19:24.413
<i>An overseas client?</i>

00:19:24.496 --> 00:19:25.539
<i>That's right.</i>

00:19:25.622 --> 00:19:29.710
If we safely recapture
what was stolen from that client,

00:19:29.793 --> 00:19:32.045
we'll get paid 50 million dollars.

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:35.090
After receiving our pay,

00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:37.634
it will be split up
among the team members.

00:19:38.218 --> 00:19:41.096
Nice. How many people does he need,
and what do we gotta do?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:44.057
I still haven't been told
about the details.

00:19:44.141 --> 00:19:48.187
But luckily, I heard there's
a spot open for one more person.

00:19:50.272 --> 00:19:52.608
Sounds good. I like it.

00:19:53.317 --> 00:19:55.944
It sure does. I thought you'd like it.

00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:58.989
Yeah. But what I like most of all,

00:19:59.698 --> 00:20:03.952
Kasey, is I get to do a job with you.

00:20:04.912 --> 00:20:06.538
It's not just any job.

00:20:06.622 --> 00:20:08.790
It's a colossally enormous job.

00:20:18.133 --> 00:20:19.551
I can hardly wait.

00:20:20.427 --> 00:20:21.845
I can't either.

00:20:31.813 --> 00:20:34.358
So where are we meeting him?

00:20:35.275 --> 00:20:36.443
Right here.

00:20:37.986 --> 00:20:38.904
What?

00:20:40.948 --> 00:20:42.282
The Heat.

00:20:47.329 --> 00:20:48.664
Seriously?

00:22:14.249 --> 00:22:19.254
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
